<article class="env-remark" id="0H6G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H6G">Remark <span data-tag="0H6G">62.13.4</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Section <a href="/tag/0H65" data-tag="0H65">62.12</a>. Let $X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes locally of finite type over $S$. Let $r \geq 0$. Let $c$ be a rule that to every morphism $g : Y' \to Y$ locally of finite type and every $e \in \mathbf{Z}$ associates an operation </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c \cap - : Z_ e(Y') \to Z_{r + e}(X')  \]
</div>
  <p> compatible with proper pushforward, flat pullback, and Gysin maps as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0H6E" data-tag="0H6E">62.13.2</a>. Then we claim there is a relative $r$-cycle $\alpha $ on $X/Y$ such that $c \cap = g^*\alpha \cap -$ for every $g$ as above. If we ever need this, we will carefully state and prove this here. </p>
</article>